            11. Frequently Asked Questions
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What is the largest portable generator you can buy?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                By output, the DuroMax XP28000iH is rated at 22,000 running and 28,000 peak watts on gasoline. By weight, the Westinghouse WGen20000TFc is the largest at 557 pounds dry, with 20,000 running watts on gasoline and natural gas capability. Both are far too heavy for one person to move easily.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What is the biggest inverter generator?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                The largest we could confirm on sale is the DuroMax XP28000iH, rated at 22,000 running watts on gasoline and 20,000 on propane. It weighs 466 pounds. The XP16000iH is a smaller option at 13,000 running watts and 368 pounds, and is listed at 66.9 dB at quarter load.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What is the largest generator one person can move?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                For most adults, about 200 to 220 pounds on large wheels across smooth ground. The Champion 201423 fits that limit at 212.3 pounds and 9,000 running watts on gasoline, in a compact 28-inch frame with 8-inch solid wheels. Anything over about 300 pounds usually needs two people.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">How heavy is a large portable generator?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Units in the 12,000 to 13,000-watt range weigh about 345 to 370 pounds dry. The 18,000 to 22,000-watt class weighs 440 to 560 pounds. A full gasoline tank adds roughly 60 to 105 pounds. One-person units top out at around 210 to 220 pounds.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Can a large portable generator run a whole house?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                A 20,000-watt unit can run most houses, including central air and electric appliances, but only if it is connected through a 100-amp transfer switch or terminal block. Through a standard 50-amp inlet, any generator is limited to 12,000 watts, which still covers most homes with some load management.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Is a heavy duty portable generator better than a standby?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                A portable costs less and can be taken elsewhere. A standby starts automatically, runs on natural gas or propane without refueling, and never has to be moved. For long or frequent outages, or households that cannot move a 450-pound machine, a standby is usually the better choice.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Do large generators need a special outlet?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Most connect to the house through a 14-50 or L14-30 inlet and a transfer switch or interlock, installed by an electrician. The 14-50 carries up to 12,000 watts and the L14-30 up to 7,200. The largest units also offer a terminal block for a 100-amp or larger connection.
              </p>
            </div>

          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Common Mistakes -->
        <div id="mistakes" class="scroll-mt-24 mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
            12. Common Mistakes to Avoid
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying the biggest generator instead of the right size</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                The largest units weigh 440 to 560 pounds and burn 1 to 2 gallons an hour. If a 9,000 to 12,000-watt unit covers your essential loads, it will be easier to store, move and run.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Assuming a large inverter is light</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                The biggest inverters are not suitcase units. The DuroMax XP28000iH weighs 466 pounds and the XP16000iH 368. Inverter technology changes noise and fuel use, not the need for two people to move it.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Ignoring the connection limit</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                A 14-50 inlet carries 12,000 watts no matter how large the generator is. To use a 20kW unit's full output, you need a 100-amp transfer switch or terminal-block connection installed by an electrician.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Planning propane runs on grill cylinders</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Large engines empty a 20 lb cylinder in a few hours. Westinghouse rates its tri-fuel unit at 3 hours at quarter load on one. Use 100 lb cylinders, a fixed tank or natural gas.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Not checking the path from storage to run spot</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Never-flat wheels work on smooth concrete. Gravel, wet grass, steps and slopes stop a 500-pound generator. Walk the route before buying and plan a pad if needed.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

